age>2305</fpage><lpage>2315</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12917450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001494-Silverman1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Silverman</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>BRG</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Translational control perks up.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>397</volume><fpage>208</fpage><lpage>211</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9930691</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001494-Ahmed1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>McKenzie</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Puckett</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hojnacki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Poliquin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Ability of the matrix protein of vesicular stomatitis virus to suppress beta interferon gene expression is genetically correlated with the inhibition of host RNA and protein synthesis.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>77</volume><fpage>4646</fpage><lpage>4657</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12663771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001494-Black1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Black</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyles</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Vesicular stomatitis virus matrix protein inhibits host cell-directed transcription of target genes in vivo.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>66</volume><fpage>4058</fpage><lpage>4064</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1318397</pub-id><